<title>GERMANY: German 1996 Q4 steel orders surge yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German 1996 Q4 steel orders surge yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office gave the following data on pan-German rolled-steel orders and deliveries:</p>
<p>(In millions of tonnes)</p>
<p>		     Q4	 Q3	 Q4	PCT CHG  PCT CHG</p>
<p>		    1996	1996    1995     QTR/QTR   YR/YR</p>
<p>ORDERS</p>
<p>  Domestic	5.423     5.702   4.603    -4.9     +17.8</p>
<p>  EU (1)	  2.260     1.882   1.496    +20.1    +51.1</p>
<p>  Others	  1.536     1.617   1.385    -5.0     +10.9</p>
<p>  TOTAL	   9.219     9.201   7.484    +0.2     +23.2</p>
<p>DELIVERIES</p>
<p>  Domestic	5.301     5.609   5.260    -5.49    +0.78</p>
<p>  EU		1.939     1.634   1.785    +18.7    +8.63</p>
<p>  Others	  1.631     1.770   1.467    -7.9     +11.18</p>
<p>  TOTAL	   8.871     9.013   8.512    -1.6     +4.2</p>
<p>ORDERS ON HAND AT END-DECEMBER 1996</p>
<p>  Domestic	4.376</p>
<p>  EU		2.051</p>
<p>  Others	  1.447</p>
<p>  TOTAL	   7.874</p>
<p>NOTE - (1) European Union excluding Germany.</p>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office said orders on hand at the end of the fourth quarter of 1996 were around eight percent above the level of the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>It added that the stronger dollar and good orders situation contributed to price rises for nearly all product segments in recent months.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
